WEBVTT

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.880
The original idea I had when I wanted to

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.160
create my first car was to also prove it

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.720
on a race car.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:15.760
>> [music]

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.960
>> The GT1 class was built around

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.360
road-going supercars, evolving some of

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.280
the world's most iconic performance

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.890
vehicles into purpose-built race cars.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:26.520
>> [music]

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.200
>> Welcome to Silverstone and the GT1

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.600
racing round two around this amazing

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.440
track. This is racing at its finest,

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.240
right, James?

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.280
>> So, the original CCGT was very much a

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.880
skunkworks Koenigsegg project. We didn't

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.680
have a big budget [music] for it. So, we

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.680
had a skeleton crew led by one of our

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.320
top engineers, Doug Belenius, who really

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.440
was a genius and had a knack of figuring

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.680
things out, reading the regulation, and

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.365
also doing the craftsmanship himself

00:00:54.365 --> 00:00:55.040
[music]

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:58.000
with only two, three people helping him

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.880
converting the chassis, the bodywork of

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.600
the CC8S and CCR into the CCGT.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.440
Unfortunately, right when we had

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.040
finished the car, they shut down the

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:08.640
series.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.440
>> Today, November 6th, 2011, marks the end

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.920
of an era. What a race, ladies and

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.240
gentlemen, the final GT1 World

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.400
Championship.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.080
>> And as a celebration of this effort, I'm

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.040
very proud and excited to introduce

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.320
>> the Koenigsegg CCGT1.

00:01:36.286 --> 00:01:38.306
>> [music]

00:01:48.731 --> 00:01:50.751
[music]

00:01:53.971 --> 00:01:55.991
[music]

00:01:59.866 --> 00:01:59.920
[music]

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.000
>> Oh.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:05.680
>> The downforce numbers are really up

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.080
there with the highest we've ever

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.080
achieved, and that's of [music] course

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.600
based on a shape of car that we

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.120
originally conceived at the end of the

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.959
'90s for the first CC8S.

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:19.600
>> Elevated with our optional track

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.200
package.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.560
>> Racing suit, helmet, [music] wheels with

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.080
slicks, different brake pad materials,

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.680
different adjustments to the shock

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.760
absorbers.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.560
>> Incorporating a motorsport developed

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.120
pneumatic air jack system.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:33.720
>> The track pack also features a carbon

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.360
fiber roll cage.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.920
>> Engineered to enable efficient

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.440
conversion from road [music] to track

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.880
use.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.420
>> The CCGT1 features the biggest rear

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.760
[music] wing we've ever made. What's

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.360
different from the original race car?

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.301
It's actually active.

00:02:50.301 --> 00:02:51.560
>> [music]

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.200
>> In front of the rear wing, a new

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.280
five-inlet roof scoop feeding air to the

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.320
engine while also providing cooling for

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.880
the light speed transmission and

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:01.440
dampers.

00:03:01.519 --> 00:03:03.200
With modern emissions regulations

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.800
eliminating the option for twin [music]

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.560
quick fuel fillers,

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.400
this area has been redesigned with

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.560
graphical readouts for fuel and oil

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.120
pressure levels for easy pit [music]

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.480
crew monitoring.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.157
>> You can also see a slightly wider stance

00:03:17.157 --> 00:03:17.760
[music]

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.239
than the CC850. The wheel arches are a

00:03:20.239 --> 00:03:21.742
little bit flared.

00:03:21.742 --> 00:03:22.200
>> [music]

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.040
>> On top of that, we have pushed our air

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.327
core technology

00:03:26.327 --> 00:03:26.600
>> [music]

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:30.519
>> to the maximum, making a retro-style

00:03:30.519 --> 00:03:33.320
looking racing [music] three-spoke

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.160
hollow carbon fiber wheel.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.760
>> Optimized air core technology, combined

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.959
with a new internal structural wall that

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:41.680
increases strength while reducing

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.640
weight, makes this one of our lightest

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.280
carbon fiber wheels ever.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.480
>> It's very much Koenigsegg thinking in a

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.120
nutshell from my perspective.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.880
>> The cockpit [music] has been redesigned

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.440
with a series of track focused

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.400
enhancements.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.240
An all new ESS sequential shifter

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.600
inspired [music] by the original

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.720
developed for the CCGT.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.040
>> Ambience of a race car with a race car

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.280
kind of switches.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:06.800
>> Placing greater emphasis [music] on

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.000
driver control, functionality, and

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.520
performance.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.120
A brand [music] new mechanical drive

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.920
mode selector. Auto, sequential, manual,

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.799
and reverse. [music]

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:21.920
Four modes, one movement.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.600
Introducing

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.440
the Chrono Cluster 3. Designed to keep

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.240
the driver fully informed with complete

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.520
visibility of the [music] car's vital

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.200
systems. And also our analog G-Force

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.103
meter seamlessly integrated.

00:04:35.103 --> 00:04:37.123
>> [music]

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.660
>> In addition to the sequential shifter,

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:42.240
[music]

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.240
the CCGT1 features an optional six-speed

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.360
gated ESS manual.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.880
>> And I remember for the first time

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.080
driving it first on our airfield, then

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.400
on Hockenheim in Germany, it was just

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.560
the most exciting thing I've ever

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.280
driven. And it's something that never

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.800
left my mind. So having the opportunity

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.680
to relive this experience now [music]

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:05.520
for our customers to experience on the

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.853
track, on the road, is just unbelievable

00:05:07.853 --> 00:05:10.680
[music] and so truly exciting to me and

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:11.720
the team.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.160
Very much looking forward to getting

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.360
these cars out [music] into the field

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.520
and being experienced.